; mh TACTICAL ORDER JOURNAL (TACT-REC)
;
; Replayed by:  python tools/test_ui.py --tact-replay <this file>
; Read directly by the DLL ([harness] tact_journal=<path>); every line that is not
; a record line is skipped, which is why this header can live in the same file.
;
;   E <frame> <unit> <op> <iflag> <arg0> <arg1> <arg2> <arg3>   unit enqueue
;   G <frame> <op> <arg0> <arg1> <arg2> <arg3>                  group order
;   D <frame> <unit> <field> <value>   direct write, no opcode exists for these:
;                                     0=active_gun 1=squad_group_id 2=def_stat
;                                     3=SELECTED (status bit 0) -- group orders
;                                       act on `status & 1`, so without it a
;                                       group order replays onto an EMPTY set
;
; INPUT -- the records that actually DRIVE a replay. Everything above is derived
; from these by the game itself, and --tact-verify holds it back as the
; expectation rather than replaying it (docs/tactical-probe.md 9p: on a real
; session all 211 derived records were re-emitted from input alone, zero shift).
;
;   M <frame> <type> <buttons> <x> <y> <dx> <dy> <wheel> <ts>   mouse event
;       type is a transition bitmask: 1=move 2=Ldown 4=Lup 8=Rdown 16=Rup
;       dx/dy/wheel are SIGNED; <ts> replays verbatim (double-click timing)
;   K <frame> <scancode> <type> <ts>                            key event
;   C <frame> <x> <y>                                           cursor position
